"""Short excerpts of two real, public club announcements (USL Championship, Dec and Nov 2025), kept so the reader
is tested on real wording. Text only; no page markup."""
RIFC_2025 = """Rhode Island FC announced on Wednesday its initial roster updates ahead of the 2026 USL Championship season, with 20 players currently under contract for the upcoming campaign.
RIFC exercised contract options for goalkeeper Koke Vegas, midfielders Amos Shapiro-Thompson and Kevin Vang, and forward JJ Williams.
The quartet join a group of 16 players previously under contract – defenders Hugo Bacharach, Grant Stoneman, Frank Nodarse, Karifa Yao, Aimé Mabika, Hamady Diop, Aldair Sanchez and Dani Rovira, midfielders Clay Holstad, Maxi Rodriguez, Zach Herivaux and Jojea Kwizera, and forwards Albert Dikwa, Noah Fuson, Mathieu Ndongo, and Dwayne Atkinson.
The club declined contract options for Cole Dewhurst, Will Meyer, Isaac Angking and Taimu Okiyoshi, while Marc Ybarra, Rio Hope-Gund and Jackson Lee are out of contract. The club also announced the retirement of Joe Brito.
Rhode Island FC goalkeeper Koke Vegas is set to return for the club's third season. | Photo courtesy Chris Cowger / Pittsburgh Riverhounds SC"""

TAMPA_2025 = """The Tampa Bay Rowdies announced the club’s roster decisions on player contract options for the 2026 USL Championship season.
The club has exercised contract options for midfielders Alex Mendez and Nate Worth for the 2026 season.
The club has declined contract options for goalkeepers Ethan Bandré and Bill Hamid, defenders Joey Skinner and Thomas Vancaeyezeele, midfielders Ollie Bassett, Danny Crisostomo, and forward Cristian Ortiz.
Forward Manuel Arteaga, midfielder Juan Carlos Azocar, midfielder Blake Bodily, midfielder Nick Moon, and midfielder Pacifique Niyongabire are all out of contract following the conclusion of the 2025 USL Championship season."""
